{"ref":"BDB, עִנְיָן","hw":"עִנְיָן","html":"† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">עִנְיָן</span></big>  <strong>n.m.</strong> <sup><a data-ref=\"Ecclesiastes 1:13\" href=\"/Ecclesiastes.1.13\">Ec 1:13</a></sup> <strong>occupation, task</strong>, only Ec <strong>(</strong>Aramaic loan-word Lag<sup>BN 205</sup>; common in NH<strong>)</strong>;—<span dir=\"rtl\">ע׳</span> abs. <a data-ref=\"Ecclesiastes 2:26\" href=\"/Ecclesiastes.2.26\">Ec 2:26</a>; <a data-ref=\"Ecclesiastes 3:10\" href=\"/Ecclesiastes.3.10\">3:10</a>; <a data-ref=\"Ecclesiastes 5:2\" href=\"/Ecclesiastes.5.2\">5:2</a>; <a data-ref=\"Ecclesiastes 8:16\" href=\"/Ecclesiastes.8.16\">8:16</a>; sf. <span dir=\"rtl\">כַּעַס עִנְיָנוֹ</span> <a data-ref=\"Ecclesiastes 2:23\" href=\"/Ecclesiastes.2.23\">2:23</a> <em>his task is</em> (sheer) <em>vexation;</em> <span dir=\"rtl\">עִנְיָן רָע</span> <a data-ref=\"Ecclesiastes 1:13\" href=\"/Ecclesiastes.1.13\">1:13</a> <em>an evil</em> (worthless) <em>task</em>, so <a data-ref=\"Ecclesiastes 4:8\" href=\"/Ecclesiastes.4.8\">4:8</a> (Mass. <span dir=\"rtl\">עִנְיַן</span> as if cstr., v. Baer<sup>1, 13</sup> but Kö<sup>ii. 1, 99</sup>), and, in weakened sense, <a data-ref=\"Ecclesiastes 5:13\" href=\"/Ecclesiastes.5.13\">5:13</a> <em>a bad business, bad affair</em>.","next":"BDB, מַעֲנָה²","prev":"BDB, עָנָה²"}